# An `X "c"` hint names the terminal of the token the lexer gives "c";
# when the parser grammar uses that token neither by name nor as a
# literal, the hint names no terminal (and could decide nothing).
# error: x_hint_unused_token.grammar:22:10:
# error: X "(" on expr → IDENT names no terminal: the parser grammar uses no token the lexer gives that text (lparen)
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    lparen
    lbrack
    rbrack
    eof
    err
'\n'                                        → skip, skip
'('                                         → lparen
'['                                         → lbrack
']'                                         → rbrack
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
exprs! = expr+                              → (exprs ...1)
expr   = IDENT X "("                        → (var 1)
       | IDENT LBRACK expr RBRACK           → (call 1 3)
       | LBRACK expr RBRACK                 → 2
